      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Traceability Model"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "One of the three main models for implementing traceability (centralized, semi-centralized, distributed), which differ mostly in how they store traceability data and share them with the relevant health authority and across actors in the supply chain."
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "Assembled from two sentences of Chapter 4 (PDF 54): 'The three main models for implementing traceability are the centralized, semi-centralized and distributed models. They differ mostly in how they store the data and share them with the relevant health authority and across actors in the supply chain.' The handbook does not state it as a definition, and recommends none of the models. Open: not adopted.",
